{
  "resourceType": "ConceptMap",
  "id": "message-omg-o19-to-bundle",
  "url": "https://ferrobridge.eu/fhir/v2mappings/ConceptMap/message-omg-o19-to-bundle",
  "name": "FerroBRIDGEOmgO19ToBundle",
  "title": "FerroBRIDGE supplement: OMG_O19 to Bundle",
  "status": "active",
  "experimental": true,
  "publisher": "Cadasto B.V. (FerroBRIDGE)",
  "description": "Adds a message map for the HL7 v2 OMG_O19 structure (O19, general clinical order; http://hl7.org/v2/StructureDefinition/OMG_O19), for which hl7.fhir.uv.v2mappings 1.0.0 ships none. The rows are those of ConceptMap/message-oml-o21-to-bundle for the segments OMG_O19 shares with OML_O21, at their OMG_O19 paths: the patient segments under PATIENT (NK1 under NEXT_OF_KIN), and the order, its request, its observations and its specimens under ORDER, where OML_O21 holds the request under ORDER.OBSERVATION_REQUEST. The OBR row into Specimen is left out, since OMG_O19 carries its specimens in the SPM that opens ORDER.SPECIMEN, which the SPM row maps. The guide ships no segment map for CTD, REL, SAC, SGH, SGT, FT1, CTI, BLG or DEV, so those stay counted as unmapped. FerroBRIDGE #637.",
